<title>ITALY: ENI's Snamprogetti 1996 profit, sales rise.</title>
<headline>ENI's Snamprogetti 1996 profit, sales rise.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-04-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italian energy group ENI's oilfield engineering arm Snamprogetti posted 1996 consolidated net profit of 114 billion lire, up 37 percent, with parent net up six percent to 86 billion lire.</p>
<p>The company said in a statement said new orders were up nine percent at 2.71 trillion lire while its existing order book was worth 4.75 trillion lire, up 10 percent on 1995.</p>
<p>Turnover was 2.147 trillion, up five percent.</p>
<p>-- Milan newsroom +392 66129589</p>
